        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q31a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=2x-2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q31a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the without-replacement branch probabilities to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(A\\mid B)=\\frac{x-1}{x+y-1}=\\frac13",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $N=x+y$. The conditional probability is defined, so $x>0$ and $N>1$. The second marble can be red after either a red or a green first marble.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{x}{N}\\times\\frac{x-1}{N-1},\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{x}{N}\\times\\frac{x-1}{N-1}+\\frac{y}{N}\\times\\frac{x}{N-1}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{x}{N}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the conditional probability formula and cancelling the nonzero factor $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{N}\\times\\frac{x-1}{N-1}}{\\frac{x}{N}}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{x-1}{N-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince this probability is $\\frac13$,\n$$\\begin{align*}3(x-1)&=N-1\\\\3(x-1)&=x+y-1\\\\y&=2x-2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 108
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q31b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
