        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q31b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "4 red marbles and 6 green marbles.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q31b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply the addition rule using ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(A\\cap B)=\\frac13P(B)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then substitute ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=2x-2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "With $N=x+y$, part (a) gives $P(A)=P(B)=\\frac{x}{N}$ and $y=2x-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=P(A\\mid B)P(B)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{x}{3N}.\\end{align*}$$\nApply the addition rule:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=\\frac{x}{N}+\\frac{x}{N}-\\frac{x}{3N}\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=\\frac{5x}{3N}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac23$,\n$$\\begin{align*}5x&=2(x+y)\\\\3x&=2y\\\\3x&=2(2x-2)\\\\x&=4\\\\y&=2(4)-2\\\\y&=6.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 4 red marbles and 6 green marbles.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
